{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834354-\u200bfae-around-the-world","id":834354,"title":"\u200bFae Around the World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-21T04:20:29-08:00","id":834354,"title":"\u200bFae Around the World","content":"With coming closer and closer of <b>Changeling</b> 2ED there are starting to show up regional Courts of all over the world. But main terms of game \u2013 like Fae, Arcadia, Wyrd and Glamour \u2013 are from Anglo-Saxon tradition. It\u2019s nothing unusual as game is written in English and some core terms must come from one mythology for integrity of game, so developers made decisions.<br /> <br /> Even then Fae and Wyrd are worldwide phenomena, so changelings comes from every culture. With regional take on Courts and Lost in 2ED, it seems logical that fae are not called that way around the world \u2013 or that there are many names for Arcadia. <b>This topic is for giving cool, regional names for those terms to use in yours stories.</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Arabic</span></b></b><br /> <b>Arcadia:</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jannah\" target=\"_blank\">Jannah</a>? ( Arabic Heaven, meaning \u201eGarden\u201d )<br /> <b>Fae: </b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jinn\" target=\"_blank\">Jinn</a><br /> <b>Glamour: </b>Si\u1e25r?<br /> <b>Hedge:</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barzakh\" target=\"_blank\">Barzakh</a><br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> Qisma<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Australian</span></b><br /> <b>Arcadia:</b> Alcheringa (Dreamtime)/Dreamtime<br /> <b>Fae:</b> Altjira (Spirits of the Alcheringa)/Royals<br /> <b>Glamour:</b> Yanda (A type of celebration)/Glam<br /> <b>Hedge:</b> Yiri (Songlines that can be used to travel long distances)/Walkabout<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> Nanga Mai (Dreams)/Nanga<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Brazil</span></span></span></b><br /> <b>Arcadia:</b> Terra das Fadas<br /> <b>Fae:</b> Fadas<br /> <b>Glamour:</b> Glamour<br /> <b>Hedge:</b> Cerca / Sebe<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> Destino / Fado<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>China</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Note: China is a very diverse nation in terms of language, culture, and religion. These are meant to be terms widely used by Changelings who speak Standard Chinese and, to one degree or another, by those who speak other varieties of Chinese. Non-Han Chinese peoples would naturally use their own terminology</i>.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Arcadia: </b>K\u016bnl\u00fan<br /> <b>Fae: </b>Xi\u0101n<br /> <b>Glamour: </b>M\u00e8il\u00ec<br /> <b>Hedge: </b>Xi\u0101nj\u00ecng<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> M\u00ecngy\u00f9n<br /> <br /> <b><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Japan</span></b></b><br /> <b>Arcadia:</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yomi\" target=\"_blank\">Yomi</a>? ( Japan Underworld )<br /> <b>Fae: </b>Yokai or Yosei<br /> <b>Glamour:</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qi\" target=\"_blank\">Qi</a><br /> <b>Hedge:</b> ???<br /> <b>Wyrd: </b>Unmei (means Destiny, Fate) or Akai Ito (means the <a href=\"http://www.faena.com/aleph/articles/the-legend-of-the-red-string-of-japan/\" target=\"_blank\">Red String of the Destiny</a>)<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sanskrit</b></span></b><br /> <b>Arcadia: </b>A\u015boka V\u0101\u1e6dik\u0101<br /> <b>Fae: </b>R\u0101k\u1e63asa<br /> <b>Glamour: </b>M\u0101y\u0101<br /> <b>Hedge: </b>Da\u1e43\u1e0daka<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> Bh\u0101gya<br /> <br /> <b><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Slavic</span></b></b><br /> <b>Arcadia:</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nav%27\" target=\"_blank\">Nawia</a><i>? </i>( Slavic Underworld )<br /> <b>Fae: </b><a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Appendix:Proto-Slavic/bog%D1%8A\" target=\"_blank\">Bogi</a> ( singular Bog )<br /> <b>Glamour:</b> <i>Blask</i> ( Shine )<br /> <b>Hedge:</b> ???<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dola_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">Dola</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Sumer</span><br /> Arcadia: </b>Kur (can mean a mountain, the underworld, the dwelling of a god, a primeval serpent, or simply a land or territory)<br /> <b>Fae:</b> Galla (a type of demon that hauls people off to the underworld)<br /> <b>Glamour: </b>Namhili (&quot;charm&quot;)<br /> <b>Hedge:</b> Kurerinkud (literally &quot;land of cedar cutting,&quot; a wilderness area inhabited by dangerous creatures in the Epic of Gilgamesh)<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> Namtar (a god or demon related to death and disease, but also sometimes regarded as the spirit of Fate - name literally means &quot;fate-cutter&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-27-2016, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T04:47:00-08:00","id":834367,"title":"","content":"A neat idea.<br /> <br /> <b><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Australian</span></b></b><br /> <b>Arcadia</b>: Alcheringa (Dreamtime)/Dreamtime<br /> <b>Fae</b>: Altjira (Spirits of the Alcheringa)/Royals<br /> <b>Wyrd</b>: Nanga Mai (Dreams)/Nanga<br /> <b>Glamour</b>: Yanda (A type of celebration)/Glam<br /> <b>Hedge</b>: Yiri (Songlines that can be used to travel long distances)/Walkabout","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-21-2016, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T05:14:40-08:00","id":834377,"title":"","content":"Here a few sugestion about Japan:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834354-\u200bfae-around-the-world#post834354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Japan</span></b></b><br /> Fae: Yokai<br /> Wyrd: <b>Unmei </b>(means Destiny, Fate) or <b>Akai Ito </b>(means the <a href=\"http://www.faena.com/aleph/articles/the-legend-of-the-red-string-of-japan/\" target=\"_blank\">Red String of the Destiny</a>)<br /> Arcadia: <b>Specific places</b> (like some forests, caverns or mountains)<br /> Glamour: <b>Chi</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The japanese myths of youkais believe that many of them live in this world, like some caverns, forests and stuff and only a few on the Yomi.<br /> The Yomi is already the land of the japanese Demons(Onis) and there's already a conspiracy of Hunters that descend from the Yomi Demons(here is the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UkJgf3IjdQuKvHmX_OxL6uBjCt02go-knYZ0Pc_UMVE/edit\" target=\"_blank\">link</a>).<br /> About the name for Glamour, I reccomend Chi, but there's probably a better name for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T05:26:44-08:00","id":834382,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we need to remember not to use any names we've already used for something else. What do the Japanese call spirits? They'd probably be kami, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T06:02:05-08:00","id":834390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834354-\u200bfae-around-the-world?p=834382#post834382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we need to remember not to use any names we've already used for something else. What do the Japanese call spirits? They'd probably be kami, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, pretty much. Spirit = Kami(\u795e). Ghost = Yurei(\u5e7d\u970a). Fairy = Yosei(\u5996\u7cbe)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T07:56:21-08:00","id":834428,"title":"","content":"The Tokyo setting in Beast The Primordial calls changelings Yosei, organized in a Yosei Court modeled after the Tale of the Bamboo Cutter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T14:49:31-08:00","id":834642,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Brazil</span></span></b><br /> <b>Arcadia:</b> Terra das Fadas<br /> <b>Fae:</b> Fadas<br /> <b>Glamour:</b> Glamour<br /> <b>Hedge:</b> Cerca / Sebe<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> Destino / Fado","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T15:32:22-08:00","id":834663,"title":"","content":"'Fado' is so very appropriate for that. The rest of the terms are likely also the exact same you'd hear in Portugal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T00:41:51-08:00","id":835632,"title":"","content":"<b>China</b><br /> <br /> Note: China is a very diverse nation in terms of language, culture, and religion. These are meant to be terms widely used by Changelings who speak Standard Chinese and, to one degree or another, by those who speak other varieties of Chinese. Non-Han Chinese peoples would naturally use their own terminology.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcadia: </b>K\u016bnl\u00fan<br /> <b>Fae: </b>Xi\u0101n<br /> <b>Glamour: </b>M\u00e8il\u00ec<br /> <b>Hedge: </b>Xi\u0101nj\u00ecng<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> M\u00ecngy\u00f9n<br /> <br /> A little explanation:<br /> <br /> K\u016bnl\u00fan is a mythical mountain said to be home to a number of deities, as well as all manner of fabulous animals and plants. What made me choose it over other, similar lands in Chinese mythology is that the name K\u016bnl\u00fan may be semantically linked to H\u00f9nd\u00f9n, a sort of cosmological term that can mean &quot;primal chaos&quot; or &quot;muddled confusion.&quot;<br /> <br /> In addition to referring to Taoist Immortals, Xi\u0101n can refer to a variety of immortal, magical beings, and in some contexts is even translated as &quot;fairy.&quot;<br /> <br /> M\u00e8il\u00ec is a pretty direct translation of &quot;glamour,&quot; meaning &quot;charisma&quot; or &quot;wonder,&quot; and is formed as a compound that could be literally read as &quot;demon power.&quot;<br /> <br /> The compound Xi\u0101nj\u00ecng is mormally glossed as &quot;fairyland,&quot; but the character \u5883 (j\u00ecng) can mean &quot;boundary&quot; or &quot;frontier&quot; as well as well as &quot;region,&quot; so it seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> M\u00ecngy\u00f9n more or less means one's personal destiny; it seems like the most appropriate word to use, but I'm certainly open to other suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 02-23-2016, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T18:57:27-08:00","id":836145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834354-\u200bfae-around-the-world?p=834377#post834377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here a few sugestion about Japan:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The japanese myths of youkais believe that many of them live in this world, like some caverns, forests and stuff and only a few on the Yomi.<br /> The Yomi is already the land of the japanese Demons(Onis) and there's already a conspiracy of Hunters that descend from the Yomi Demons(here is the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UkJgf3IjdQuKvHmX_OxL6uBjCt02go-knYZ0Pc_UMVE/edit\" target=\"_blank\">link</a>).<br /> About the name for Glamour, I reccomend Chi, but there's probably a better name for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some additional thoughts on the subject:<br /> <br /> Japan has a term for the phenomena of being abducted by gods or supernatural beings- Kamikakushi (&quot;hidden by the Kami [gods; spirits]&quot; usually translated into English as being &quot;Spirited Away&quot; (yes, the Miyazaki film of the same name provides an excellent example of the concept). A related term, Onikakushi, specifically refers to the abduction of a person by an Oni or demon and is usually translated as being &quot;demoned away&quot;. It has interesting parallels to the western concept of children being stolen by the fairies. I imagine that in the Chronicles of Darkness a japanese changeling will typically refer to their experience in these terms.<br /> <br /> And while I'm on the subject, here's an article from wikipedia <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yama-bito\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yama-bito</a><br /> <br /> I'm noticing another parallel between Western theories about fairy legends referring to minorities living in the hills on the fringes of modern civilization and these Yamabito. Perhaps a general term for Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T22:42:05-08:00","id":836252,"title":"","content":"I had a few thoughts on some possible Arabic Changeling terminology:<br /> <br /> For Glamour, an appropriate term might be <b>Si\u1e25r</b>, which literally means &quot;magic,&quot; but has connotations of deception and fascination. That said, si\u1e25r is, properly speaking, a verbal noun, and this refers to the act of performing magic, rather than magic as any kind of entity in-and-of itself. I'm certainly open to suggestions for a term that might better describe magical or emotional power or energy.<br /> <br /> If we're going with Jannah for Arcadia, then <b>Barzakh</b> might make sense for the Hedge. The word literally means &quot;obstacle&quot; or &quot;partition,&quot; or, in Geography, an isthmus, but in at least some branches of Islam it can also specifically refer to a barrier between the material and spiritual worlds, in which the human soul dwells between a person's death and the Day of Judgement.<br /> <br /> For Wyrd, <b>Qisma</b> is a term that can mean &quot;allotment&quot; or &quot;fate,&quot; and is the ultimate origin of the word &quot;Kismet.&quot; This is probably preferable to <b>Q</b><b>adr</b>, which specifically refers to predestination and the will of God. For a more anthropomorphic conception of the Wyrd, it might be appropriate to use <b>al-Q\u0101sim</b>, &quot;the divider&quot; or &quot;the distributor,&quot; as in one who meets out each person's allotment. This is, naturally, related to qisma; Arabic and other Semitic languages tend to form words with related meanings by inserting different vowels into a root consisting of three consonants, in this case q-s-m.<br /> <br /> And now, just for fun:<br /> <br /> <b>Sumer<br /> <br /> Arcadia: </b>Kur (can mean a mountain, the underworld, the dwelling of a god, a primeval serpent, or simply a land or territory)<br /> <b>Fae:</b> Galla (a type of demon that hauls people off to the underworld)<br /> <b>Glamour: </b>Namhili (&quot;charm&quot;)<br /> <b>Hedge:</b> Kurerinkud (literally &quot;land of cedar cutting,&quot; a wilderness area inhabited by dangerous creatures in the Epic of Gilgamesh)<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> Namtar (a god or demon related to death and disease, but also sometimes regarded as the spirit of Fate - name literally means &quot;fate-cutter&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T07:04:45-08:00","id":837005,"title":"","content":"Not sure on the other terms but for the Philippines, <b>Engkanto</b> sounds right for the Fae. The translation is vague but it's generally means a fairy or an elf like being. Changelings might be called <b>Engkantao </b>which is a term used for a half fairy/half elf or a descendant of an Engkanto which also works with the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6163-yama951","name":"Yama951","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T15:43:49-08:00","id":837804,"title":"","content":"<b>Sanskrit</b><br /> <br /> So, the cultures and languages of India are far too diverse for there to be any one set of &quot;Indian&quot; terms for Changeling-related stuff. These terms are from Sanskrit, and represent ways in which some Hindu and Buddhist changelings, particularly in South and Southeast Asia, might talk about their experiences. Sanskrit has a very rich body of literature to draw on, but these terms specifically allude to the <i>Ramayana</i>, as I felt that many lost in this part of the world would feel a kinship with Sita, the wife of Rama whose abduction to a distant land forms the central conflict of the epic.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcadia: </b>A\u015boka V\u0101\u1e6dik\u0101<br /> <b>Fae: </b>R\u0101k\u1e63asa<br /> <b>Glamour: </b>M\u0101y\u0101<br /> <b>Hedge: </b>Da\u1e43\u1e0daka or Da\u1e43\u1e0dakara\u1e47ya<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> Bh\u0101gya<br /> <br /> Some Explanation:<br /> <br /> In the <i>Ramayana</i>, A\u015boka V\u0101\u1e6dik\u0101 is the name of a garden where Sita dwells after her abduction by Ravana, preferring to dwell under an <i>A\u015boka</i> tree rather than in the palace of her captor.<br /> <br /> The R\u0101k\u1e63asa are a race of shape-changers who have the power of M\u0101y\u0101. In the <i>Ramayana</i>, Ravana is the king of the R\u0101k\u1e63asa, and Rama and his allies must make war on the monsters in order to rescue Sita.<br /> <br /> M\u0101y\u0101 is a term with a number of different meanings in Hindu literature, but most often refers to sorcery, illusion, and deception. Conversely, it can also sometimes mean compassion or sympathy, and in the earliest Sanskrit texts it refers to art, wisdom, or extraordinary supernatural power.<br /> <br /> Da\u1e43\u1e0daka is a vast primeval forest that appears on the Ramayana and a number of other Hindu texts, a dangerous land inhabited only by isolated hermits and teeming with dangerous animals and supernatural beings. Rama, Sita, and Rama's brother Lakshmana dwelt there in exile for 14 years, and it was here that Sita was abducted by Ravana and carried away to the south.<br /> <br /> The term Bh\u0101gya basically just means &quot;fate&quot; or &quot;chance.&quot; I was tempted to use the word \u1e5ata, which refers to the natural order of the universe, but that concept has a moral dimension that I don't think really fits with the way the Wyrd functions.<br /> <br /> As a bonus, <b>Vidy\u0101</b> is a term that Hindu Changelings might use for Clarity, meaning &quot;true knowledge,&quot; which purifies and uplifts an individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 02-27-2016, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:24:20-07:00","id":856574,"title":"","content":"So, based on the Three Kingdoms era from <i>Dark Eras</i>, some adjustments to our Chinese Changeling terminology may be in order.<br /> <br /> At least during that era, the common term for Arcadia was <b>Ko\u0304ngd\u00f2ng</b>, meaning roughly &quot;the hollow.&quot;<br /> <br /> The True Fey, on the other hand, fall under the admittedly broad category of <b>Y\u0101ogu\u00e0i</b>, which encompasses all sorts of strange monsters and evil spirits and the like. This seems reasonable enough, since the Fair Folk are diverse enough in form and motivation that not all cultures will necessarily identify them as a single, narrow class of being.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Changelings of China seem to equate the Wyrd with the will of Heaven, which makes a fair amount of sense given the role the concept plays in Chinese philosophy. The most straightforward term for Wyrd would therefore be <b>Ti\u0101n</b>, &quot;heaven.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:32:06-07:00","id":856577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834354-\u200bfae-around-the-world#post834354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Arabic</span></b></b><br /> <b>Arcadia:</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jannah\" target=\"_blank\">Jannah</a>? ( Arabic Heaven, meaning \u201eGarden\u201d )<br /> <b>Fae: </b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jinn\" target=\"_blank\">Jinn</a><br /> <b>Glamour: </b>Si\u1e25r?<br /> <b>Hedge:</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barzakh\" target=\"_blank\">Barzakh</a><br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> Qisma</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go for Qaf instead of Jannah, as Qaf (Cafcuh in Farsi) is a domain of Jinn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}